capability xlsx/cell-names  a cell's name, `B3`, turned into its row and column and back; column letters; areas `A1:C3`
  heroes  xlsx.parse_cell_name, xlsx.format_cell_name, xlsx.parse_column_name, xlsx.format_column_name, xlsx.parse_area, xlsx.format_area, xlsx.Position, xlsx.Area, xlsx.is_before
  go      excelize.CellNameToCoordinates, CoordinatesToCellName, ColumnNameToNumber, ColumnNumberToName, SplitCellName, JoinCellName
  rust    rust_xlsxwriter::utility::column_name_to_number, column_number_to_name, row_col_to_cell, row_col_to_cell_absolute, cell_range, cell_range_absolute, worksheet_range, worksheet_range_absolute, quote_sheet_name, check_sheet_name, check_name, ColNum, RowNum
  python  openpyxl.utils.cell.get_column_letter, column_index_from_string, coordinate_from_string, coordinate_to_tuple, absolute_coordinate, range_boundaries, range_to_tuple, rows_from_range, cols_from_range, get_column_interval, quote_sheetname, COORD_RE, ABSOLUTE_RE, RANGE_EXPR, COL_RANGE, ROW_RANGE, SHEETRANGE_RE, SHEET_TITLE, CellCoordinatesException, CellRange (every attribute), Cell.coordinate, Cell.row, Cell.column, Cell.col_idx, Cell.column_letter, Cell.offset, CellRange.bottom, coord, cols, max_col, min_col, expand, shrink, shift, intersection, union, isdisjoint, issubset, issuperset
  note    rows and columns count from 0, as calamine and rust_xlsxwriter, so a row is an index into `rows_of`; excelize and openpyxl count from 1; a sheet's name in a reference is quoted by the program

capability xlsx/write  a workbook written to a file, a stream or bytes in memory
  heroes  xlsx.save, xlsx.write, xlsx.to_bytes
  go      excelize.NewFile, File.Save, File.SaveAs, File.Write, File.WriteTo, File.WriteToBuffer, File.SetZipWriter, excelize.ZipWriter
  rust    Workbook::new, Workbook.save, save_to_buffer, save_to_writer, set_zip_compression_level, use_zip_large_file
  python  openpyxl.Workbook, Workbook.save, openpyxl.writer, Workbook.template, Workbook.mime_type, Worksheet.mime_type
  note    the same workbook gives the same bytes: every member is stamped 1980-01-01, as rust_xlsxwriter does; texts go to the shared strings, as Excel and rust_xlsxwriter write them, where openpyxl writes them inline

capability xlsx/build-sheets  sheets added to a workbook, named, hidden, the one shown first chosen
  heroes  xlsx.new_workbook, xlsx.new_sheet, xlsx.add_sheet, xlsx.Sheet (visibility), xlsx.Workbook (active)
  go      File.NewSheet, File.SetSheetName, File.SetSheetVisible, File.SetActiveSheet
  rust    Workbook.add_worksheet, push_worksheet, worksheet_from_index, worksheet_from_name, worksheets, worksheets_mut, Worksheet::new, Worksheet.name, set_name, set_active, set_hidden, set_very_hidden, set_first_tab, set_selected
  python  Workbook.create_sheet, Worksheet.title, Worksheet.sheet_state, Workbook.active
  note    the sheet shown first may not be hidden, which Excel requires and `write` checks; names are compared in any case of ASCII letters, as Excel compares them

capability xlsx/sheet-edit  sheets removed, copied, moved; rows and columns inserted, removed, duplicated, an area moved, the references of formulas moved with them
  heroes  pending
  go      File.DeleteSheet, File.CopySheet, File.MoveSheet, File.GroupSheets, File.UngroupSheets, File.InsertRows, File.RemoveRow, File.InsertCols, File.RemoveCol, File.DuplicateRow, File.DuplicateRowTo, File.UpdateLinkedValue
  rust    -
  python  Workbook.remove, Workbook.remove_sheet, Workbook.copy_worksheet, Workbook.move_sheet, Worksheet.insert_rows, delete_rows, insert_cols, delete_cols, move_range
  note    rows and columns inserted or removed move the references of every formula and defined name that names them, which needs `xlsx/formulas-read`'s mover across sheets; a sheet removed or moved is `lists.remove_at` and `lists.insert` on `Workbook.sheets`, with nothing to keep the defined names and `active` in step

capability xlsx/write-values  cells written with a type: number, text, boolean, error, empty; a whole row at once
  heroes  xlsx.set_value, xlsx.add_row, xlsx.Value
  go      File.SetCellValue, File.SetCellStr, SetCellInt, SetCellUint, SetCellFloat, SetCellBool, SetCellDefault, SetSheetRow, SetSheetCol
  rust    Worksheet.write, write_number, write_string, write_boolean, write_blank, write_row, write_column, write_row_matrix, write_column_matrix, clear_cell, clear_cell_format, set_nan_value, set_infinity_value, set_neg_infinity_value, IntoExcelData, every `_with_format` twin, Worksheet.write_with_format, write_number_with_format, write_string_with_format, write_boolean_with_format, write_row_with_format, write_column_with_format
  python  Worksheet.cell, Cell.value, Worksheet.append, Worksheet.__setitem__
  note    a NaN or an infinity fails `unsupported`: the format has no number for it, where rust_xlsxwriter writes a text or an error in its place; a text past 32,767 characters fails `invalid`, as rust_xlsxwriter refuses it; a control character is written `_xHHHH_`, as Excel writes it, where openpyxl refuses it

capability xlsx/write-dates  dates and times written as serial numbers with a date format, by the workbook's epoch
  heroes  xlsx.set_value (a `.date`), xlsx.Workbook (epoch)
  go      File.SetCellValue (a time.Time), File.SetWorkbookProps (Date1904), WorkbookPropsOptions
  rust    Worksheet.write_datetime, write_datetime_with_format, ExcelDateTime, ExcelDateTime.new_value, to_string_value, write_with_format
  python  Cell.value (a datetime, date or time), Workbook.epoch
  note    a date whose style shows no date is given `yyyy-mm-dd`, or `yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss` where it has a time, as openpyxl gives its own (`yyyy-mm-dd h:mm:ss`), so it reads back as a date

capability xlsx/write-formulas  a formula written as text, its last value given or left for Excel to compute on opening
  heroes  xlsx.set_formula
  go      File.SetCellFormula, FormulaOpts, File.SetCalcProps, File.GetCalcProps, CalcPropsOptions
  rust    Worksheet.write_formula, write_formula_with_format, set_formula_result, set_formula_result_default, write_array_formula, write_dynamic_formula, write_dynamic_array_formula (and their `_with_format` twins), Formula, Formula.new, set_result, Workbook.set_calculation_mode, CalculationMode, Worksheet.write_array_formula_with_format, write_dynamic_formula_with_format, write_dynamic_array_formula_with_format, Formula.new_value, to_string_value, write_with_format, CalculationMode.Automatic, Manual, Partial
  python  Cell.value (a text opening with `=`), openpyxl.worksheet.formula.ArrayFormula, Worksheet.array_formulae, Workbook.calculation
  note    a workbook holding a formula asks Excel to compute every formula on opening (`fullCalcOnLoad`), as openpyxl; a value set beside the formula is written as its last result, as rust_xlsxwriter's set_formula_result; array and dynamic array formulas are written as ordinary ones, and a calculation mode is not chosen

